    ///   - id: The session ID of the recording whose transcription failed.
    ///   - audioURL: On-disk URL of the preserved audio file.
    /// - Throws: A storage error if the underlying persistence layer fails.
    func markNeedsRetranscription(id: RecordingID, audioURL: URL) async throws

    /// Clears the needs-retranscription flag after a retry succeeds (#326).
    ///
    /// Without this, `markNeedsRetranscription` is a one-way door: a single
    /// transcription failure would mean the recording is picked up by
    /// `RecoverPendingSessionsUseCase` and re-transcribed at every launch forever.
    /// Call this ONLY after the retried transcript has been persisted successfully —
    /// if the retry fails again, the flag must stay set so the session is retried
    /// on the next launch too (bounded-retry backoff is out of scope for #326).
    ///
    /// - Parameter id: The identifier of the recording whose flag should be cleared.
    func clearNeedsRetranscription(id: RecordingID) async throws
}

